WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.130
In 2008, the UK economy started to shrink.

2
00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:07.340
It kept shrinking for
five quarters in a row.

3
00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:10.100
Output fell by more than 6 per cent.

4
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:13.520
It took five years to
get back to its old size.

5
00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:17.590
Yet over decades, the economy's
capacity keeps rising.

6
00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:20.680
So why does an economy
grow in bursts and slumps

7
00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:22.920
instead of at a steady pace?

8
00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:25.220
In this mission, you'll map the cycle,

9
00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:28.710
phase by phase, and measure
the gap from the trend.

10
00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:31.480
Then you'll use a graph lab to open a gap,

11
00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:34.400
and watch output and the price level move.

12
00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:38.530
Your mission: find out what
makes an economy boom and slump.
